format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

objective u2-particle-or-wave
statement: Know that alpha and beta are particles and gamma is electromagnetic radiation, so the three are different.
misconception: Alpha, beta and gamma are the same thing, and gamma is made of tiny pieces of the nucleus.

item u2-l2-choice-gamma-element
type: choice
difficulty: 2
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-radiation-types

prompt:
    A gamma ray leaves a nucleus. Does the nucleus turn into a different element?

options:
    {"id":"no","label":"No: a gamma ray is not a particle, so no protons leave"}
    {"id":"yes-protons","label":"Yes: it loses protons","note":"Gamma is electromagnetic radiation. No protons or neutrons leave."}
    {"id":"yes-always","label":"Yes: every decay changes the element","note":"Gamma carries energy away and does not change the number of protons."}

answer: no

explanation:
    No. Gamma is electromagnetic radiation, not a particle, so no protons or neutrons leave. The nucleus stays the same element.

item u2-l2-sort-kind
type: sort
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-radiation-types

prompt:
    Is it a particle, or electromagnetic radiation? Sort each one.

buckets:
    {"id":"particle","label":"A particle","icon":"AqParticle"}
    {"id":"em","label":"Electromagnetic radiation","icon":"AqWave"}

items:
    {"id":"alpha","label":"Alpha","bucket":"particle"}
    {"id":"beta","label":"Beta","bucket":"particle"}
    {"id":"gamma","label":"Gamma","bucket":"em"}
    {"id":"light","label":"Visible light","bucket":"em"}

explanation:
    Alpha and beta are particles. Gamma and visible light are electromagnetic radiation, and gamma carries far more energy.

item u2-l2-tom-light
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-radiation-types

statement:
    Visible light is electromagnetic radiation, just like gamma rays.

answer: true

explanation:
    True. Light and gamma rays are both electromagnetic radiation. Gamma rays carry far more energy.

item u2-l2-tom-pieces
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-radiation-types

statement:
    Gamma radiation is made of tiny pieces of the nucleus.

answer: myth

explanation:
    Myth. Gamma is electromagnetic radiation, like light but far more energetic. It is not made of pieces of the nucleus.

item u2-l2-tom-same
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-radiation-types

statement:
    Alpha, beta and gamma are three versions of the same thing.

answer: myth

explanation:
    Myth. Alpha and beta are different particles, and gamma is electromagnetic radiation, not a particle. They are three different things.

item u2-x-not-particle
type: choice
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-radiation-types

prompt:
    Which of these is not a particle?

options:
    {"id":"gamma","label":"Gamma radiation"}
    {"id":"alpha","label":"An alpha particle","note":"Alpha is a particle."}
    {"id":"beta","label":"A beta particle","note":"Beta is a particle."}

answer: gamma

explanation:
    Gamma radiation is electromagnetic radiation, not a particle.

item u2-x-tom-particles
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-iaea-radiation-types

statement:
    Alpha and beta are particles.

answer: true

explanation:
    True. Alpha is 2 protons and 2 neutrons and beta is a fast electron. Gamma is the one that is not a particle.
